  "verified_against": {
    "source": "release-manifest.json",
    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.43.0 release assets and hashed independently, then checked again by re-fetching the URL this pin itself names. Only the pegasus artifact changed: install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.28.0 and earlier. v5.43.0 reaches this distribution through its command surface and through the screen a person configures models from, so it changes what an operator types and what they see under DARQ's own names. Configuring several things used to fire one command per item, and each command consumed a snapshot generation and re-rendered the whole configuration: four models were four renders of every artifact, four generations and four notices for one sitting, and with five generations kept that alone erased the restore history. Now the batch-capable commands take several arguments at once and the models screen stages what it is told and applies it on a confirm, the way the MCP screen already did -- one intention, one command, one generation, one render. The command surface changed with it: models set takes a repeatable --assign AGENT=PROVIDER/MODEL and a repeatable --effort AGENT=LEVEL, and --agent with --model is gone. Each flag names the agent it belongs to rather than pairing by position between two separately repeated flags, because that implicit relation is not something argparse validates and a misalignment would pass in silence. A batch with one bad item refuses entirely, names which one, and writes nothing -- including a case an adversarial review found and reproduced by running it, where a removal that failed to apply stayed written anyway. Every generation now records which command produced it, read as optional so the generations written before that field existed go on reading; twenty are kept instead of five, which measured under two megabytes on a real installation; and restore --list finally shows which ones exist, since until now restore asked for a number with no way to discover it. This distribution changed nothing of its own for this pin beyond the alignment."
  }
}
